{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Limbs (a) and (d) of POL-NS-01 are both on the record. The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-08-05T10:16:33+08:00, the trip shows no boarding event anywhere, and it is terminated by the driver at 10:23:23 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW - one of the three codes limb (d) recognises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "events[driver_arrived]",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (b) is satisfied and the POL-NS-02 arrival test is passed. The driver's own trace places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at the very moment of the arrival event: the first qualifying in-geofence fix is stamped 10:16:33 with dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0, his closest fix is 0.0 m from the pin, and 42 of his 86 fixes qualify inside the radius - far beyond POL-NS-02's three-consecutive-fix minimum, and established on admissible fixes rather than asserted proximity.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03305", "EV-TRIP-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (c) is satisfied with a large margin. The driver held position inside the geofence for a continuous 410 seconds - 42 consecutive qualifying fixes from 10:16:33 to 10:23:23 - against a free waiting period of 180 seconds in force for this trip under trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec. Measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, as POL-NS-01(c) requires and not from the arrival tap, the derived shortfall is -230 seconds: a surplus, not a shortfall. A dwell of 410 seconds also clears the 300 second legacy STANDARD figure in the fee_schedule table on any view.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03305", "EV-TRIP-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-05 does not fire against this driver. The arrival marker is a BUTTON press, and that clause asks only whether the driver was more than 300 m from the pin or travelling at 15 km/h or more at that moment. He was not: the first qualifying in-geofence fix coincides with the 'I'm Here' tap at 10:16:33, dwell_start_offset_sec is 0.0, and the trace shows him stationary inside the radius for the whole run. The waiting clock is therefore the one the platform started, not a recomputed one.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03305", "EV-TRIP-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-06 cannot rescue the rider. The dwell here is a single continuous in-geofence interval of 410 seconds, so there is no second interval for limb (i) to sum and accumulation is unnecessary; and the only advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-03305-01, is MISSING - the identifier is minted but the payload is absent, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. I disclose that impairment expressly. Its absence is citable and it changes nothing: no advisory is needed to excuse a shortfall, because there is no shortfall, and POL-NS-06(ii)'s rule that an advisory never reduces the required minimum is not reached.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-03305-01", "EV-GPS-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 fails at limb (c) on the rider's own record. Her device was never at the pin: her track runs 10:13:58 to 10:23:56 at a minimum distance of 848.5 m and a mean of 852.3 m from the pickup pin, roughly 850 m outside the 100 m rider-presence radius for a STANDARD zone, and rider_qualifying_fix_count is 0. Limb (c) is affirmatively failed on admissible fixes, so by that clause's own terms POL-NS-04 does not apply and the dispute is decided under POL-NS-01. The rider's chat message at 10:18:53 does not change that: she was still never within 100 m of the vehicle.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03305", "EV-CHAT-03305", "EV-TRIP-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-03 is not this case. That clause allocates a driver who held position OUTSIDE the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin - the wrong-entrance, wrong-face-of-the-building scenario. This driver's fixes sit inside the 50 m radius, so there is no mislocation to attribute to either party, no platform-funded pin-ambiguity goodwill under POL-NS-03(ii), and no basis for a refund under that clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03305", "EV-TRIP-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the profiles engages POL-NS-09. Both counterparty counters are 0, so there are not the 2 or more same-rider-same-driver no-show disputes in 90 days that limb (c) requires; and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, far below the 3 limb (d) requires. There is no contradicting artifact on arrival, dwell or rider presence: the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare ledger agree. There is no route to human review here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-03305", "EV-DPROF-03305", "EV-GPS-03305", "EV-TRIP-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The anti-farming guard of POL-NS-07 does not trip, because it requires BOTH limbs and only one is met. no_show_terminations_30d is 4, which satisfies the count limb; but the rate limb fails, since 4 divided by completed_trips_30d (60) is 0.067, below the 0.08 threshold. Compensation is therefore payable and not withheld. The lifetime counter prior_no_show_flags (9) is expressly not the field this check reads and is not relied on here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On a verified no-show, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of the cancellation fee in force: 80 percent of SGD 4.50 is SGD 3.60, and that is exactly the figure the fare ledger's own derived money block computes as driver_compensation. The driver drove to the pickup, waited the full free period and 230 seconds beyond it, and the ruling should say so in cash.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03305", "EV-TRIP-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fee line reconciles and there is no integrity defect to exploit. platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd is 4.50 and the fare_breakdown cancellation_fee line is 4.50, with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.0 - squarely within POL-NS-08(d)'s allowance. The rider's 'only a few minutes late' does not describe this record: the free waiting period she paid for had already expired by 230 seconds when the driver cancelled, and the chat shows the driver asking for her at 10:16:58 and her replying only at 10:18:53, after which she still had not appeared 4 minutes 30 seconds later.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03305", "EV-TRIP-03305", "EV-CHAT-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The disposition the record supports is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, not NO_ACTION on the driver: POL-NS-07 pays the driver where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, which is this case. Under POL-GEN-03 the rider's claim is not supported and the present charge stands as it is, while the emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 3.60.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03305", "EV-TRIP-03305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.6,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee stands, and the driver is paid SGD 3.60 by the platform.\n\nWHY THE FEE STANDS. POL-NS-01 requires four things and all four are on the record. (a) The trip record carries the driver's 'I'm Here' arrived event at 2026-08-05T10:16:33+08:00. (b) The GPS trace (EV-GPS-03305, weight 1.0) places the car inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at that same moment: the first qualifying in-geofence fix is stamped 10:16:33, at 0.0 m from the pin (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0), with 42 of 86 fixes qualifying inside the radius — far beyond POL-NS-02's three-consecutive-fix minimum, and on admissible fixes rather than asserted proximity. (c) He then held position continuously for 410 seconds, from 10:16:33 to 10:23:23, against the free waiting period of 180 seconds in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec; no_show_threshold_sec is null). Measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix as the clause directs, that is a surplus of 230 seconds, not a shortfall. (d) No boarding event is recorded and the trip was terminated by the driver at 10:23:23 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes the limb recognises, at or after the required dwell elapsed. POL-NS-05 does not fire: at the arrival tap the car was at the pin, not more than 300 m away and not travelling at 15 km/h or more, so the platform's own waiting clock stands and no recomputation is required.\n\nTHE RIDER'S POINTS. Your 'only a few minutes late' is not what the record shows: the 180-second free waiting period had already expired 230 seconds before the driver cancelled, and the chat shows the driver asking for you at 10:16:58 with your reply 'coming down now' at 10:18:53 — a further 4 minutes 30 seconds before cancellation, and you never reached the vehicle. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate you. Even accepting that limbs (a) and (b) are made out (your message is a coordinating one and the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor placed an in-app call — trip_record.in_app_calls is empty), limb (c) is affirmatively failed on your own track: your device sits about 850 m from the pin for every fix in the window (minimum 848.5 m, mean 852.3 m, zero of your 67 fixes inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius). POL-NS-04 says in terms that where limb (c) is affirmatively failed the clause does not apply and the dispute is decided under POL-NS-01. The chat message records that you said you were coming down; it does not place you at the pickup, and the clause reads rider position from the rider_track. POL-NS-03 (wrong-entrance) is not this case either: the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the 50 m radius, not outside it, so there is no mislocation to attribute and no pin-ambiguity goodwill. POL-NS-06 does not assist you: there is no shortfall for it to excuse, and the only traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-03305-01) is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, which both sides disclosed — a missing advisory makes limb (i) unavailable and can never extend or reduce the required minimum in any event.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S COMPENSATION. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so POL-NS-07 fixes your payout at 80 percent of the fee in force: 0.8 x SGD 4.50 = SGD 3.60, the same figure the fare ledger's derived money block computes (derived.money.driver_compensation). The anti-farming guard does not trip, because it requires both limbs: no_show_terminations_30d is 4 (count limb met) but 4 divided by 60 completed trips in 30 days is 0.067, which is not greater than the 0.08 the clause requires. The lifetime counter prior_no_show_flags (9) was mentioned in the driver's claim but is a context-only field under POL-GEN-01; it is not the field the check reads and no finding rests on it.\n\nNO ESCALATION. No POL-NS-09 trigger is met. The same-pair counters (rider_profile and driver_profile disputes_with_counterparty_90d) are both 0, so limb (c) is not reached; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the 3 limb (d) names; the trip record, GPS trace and fare ledger agree on arrival, dwell and termination, so there is no limb (b) conflict, and a clause (POL-NS-04(c), read with POL-NS-11) governs rider presence; and no deciding fact rests on an artifact impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d) — the trace has 100 percent coverage, no gaps, and the fare line reconciles to the SGD 4.50 produced by the resolution rule. Because the ruling does not rest on any artifact below weight 1.0, no POL-GEN-02(3) discount note is required beyond naming EV-ADVIS-03305-01 above, whose absence carries no fact anyway.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND EXECUTION. Confidence is 0.95, within the cap set by the deciding artifacts EV-GPS-03305 and EV-TRIP-03305, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, and well above the 0.70 platform-wide floor. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 automatic execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so it executes on issue. No clause directs a referral in this case: the arrival marker was true, so POL-NS-05(ii) does not apply, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming guard does not trip. Under POL-GEN-03 the rider's claim is not supported and the charge remains as it currently stands; the emitted ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 3.60."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

